    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG a delighted to present to the market 62 Kilmore Drive, a well-proportioned three bedroom home offering a wonderful opportunity for buyers looking to put their own stamp on a property. While the house would benefit from some updating and modernisation, it has excellent bones, generous accommodation and a layout that provides a fantastic foundation for creating a comfortable and attractive family home..\n\nAccommodation consists of entrance porch which leads into a welcoming hallway, two well proportioned reception rooms, providing excellent flexibility for use as separate living and dining spaces, a home office or additional family accommodation. To the rear, the breakfast room leads through to the kitchen, which is situated in an extension of the home. A downstairs shower room adds useful convenience, while the garage provides valuable storage space and is accessed externally. \n\nTo the first floor are three bedrooms, together with a family bathroom, offering practical accommodation for families, couples or those requiring additional space for guests or working from home.\n\nExternally, the front garden provides off street car parking. To the rear is a particularly attractive mature garden which has been well maintained and enjoys a desirable south facing aspect. \n\nKilmore Drive is a quiet, mature neighbourhood surrounded by a host of local amenities, a short drive to Dublin City Centre, Dublin Airport, Beaumont Hospital and neighbouring villages such as Malahide, Howth, Raheny and Clontarf. Local amenities such as the St Anne's Park, Dollymount Beach, Artane Castle S.C., Northside S.C., and Clare Hall S.C. are all within a 5-minute drive. A large well kept green area is a located at the bottom of the road and offers an excellent place for kids to play or to go for a walk. Excellent public transport links are on the doorstep providing direct access to the City Centre with the M50 and M1 motorways a 5-minute drive away.\n\nViewing comes highly recommended."
      },
      {
